I didn't answer the question. It's Q-1, "What must a lent book have?", at the actions stage. Answers are recorded as your own words, and a person has to confirm the elements built from them. If I made up an answer, it would go into the record as yours. I also have nothing about the library domain to base one on.

I've messaged you a default to approve with one word. A lent book would have:
- a borrower;
- a due date;
- a status of "lent".

It could only be lent if it is currently available. You can reply "ok" to use that or send your own wording. Once you reply, I'll record it as your answer and propose the elements from it.
